Appendix G — Open Problems

The following are stated as open, not as solved or as corollaries.

G-1 (Order-robustness characterization).
Is (OR-Xu) decidable for a finitely presented Datalog fragment in time polynomial in $|S_O|+|E_{\mathcal{H}}|$? By C-2, no acyclicity condition suffices; a decision procedure must detect symmetric derivation cycles between essential atoms, which is a graph property of the implication hypergraph, not a syntactic property of the program. The framework does not settle whether this is polynomial.

G-2 (All-SCC complexity).
Allamigeon (2014) establishes a superlinear lower bound for all-SCC in directed hypergraphs and almost-linear terminal SCCs. Is there a natural restricted class (e.g. bounded-arity hypergraphs, or hypergraphs with bounded König deficiency) on which all-SCC is almost-linear? The framework's Choice B (§3.4) does not require this, but a positive answer would upgrade the confusable-block partition from a structural diagnostic to a usable algorithmic object.

G-3 (Hypergraph entropy evaluation).
Xu (§III-C) characterizes the confusable-core rate via hypergraph entropy under pairwise realisability. Explicit computation of this quantity for a corpus of non-toy size is not addressed here. This is a rate-theoretic problem, external to the framework.

G-4 (Persistent watermarks and (NR)/(WM)).
The framework treats (NR) and (WM) as hypotheses. A natural open question is whether a CRDT exists satisfying (RD), add-wins semantics for the OR component, and a proof of (NR) or (WM) from the algebra alone, without a persistent watermark. The literature on δ-CRDTs and stability-based pruning suggests this is achievable only with a delivery-layer assumption on the network; whether a purely algebraic construction suffices is open.

G-5 (Epoch-lattice thresholds).
The evidence threshold $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{threshold}}$ of Def. 7.1 is a protocol parameter, not a derived quantity. The framework does not specify how the threshold is chosen, nor whether its choice can be made monotone-invariant under merge. This is an open design question.

G-6 (Codec soundness).
The coboundary defect $\|\delta x\|_1$ and the harmonic residual of Algorithm 2 are metrics on $C^0$; the framework does not prove that the decoded report under a rate-$R(0)$ code has $\|\delta x\|_1$ bounded by the distortion under which the encoder operates. Connecting the codec defect to the rate-distortion guarantee is open and would require a distortion-fidelity bridge that the present framework does not construct.

G-7 (Machine-checked status).
None of the Lean targets in Appendix E are discharged. Until E-1 through E-8 are checked, Appendix A's "Complete" entries are paper-and-pencil. E-9's refutation witnesses are strongly recommended as a first target, because they lock in the regression against the earlier draft's errors.

